  "rationale": "structural: The text prescribes two structural points. (1) The signature: `pub fn ask<R>(&self) -> Ask<'_, 'd, D, R, ContextPhase> where R: DeserializeOwned + JsonSchema + Send`, in `impl<'d, D: Domain> ValidationContext<'d, D>`. `crates/trust-but-verify/src/procedure.rs#impl[ValidationContext<'d, D>]#3/fn[ask]` declares exactly this signature, with the same lifetimes, return type and bounds. It carries the `{impl}` marker. (2) \"Its graph tools share the dependency list used by direct reads\". An alternative that builds the `Ask` over a fresh or cloned context would keep the signature but break sharing. The root avoids this: it stores `ctx: self`, a borrowed `&ValidationContext`, in `Ask`. `Ask::execute` (`impl[Ask<'a, 'd, D, R, P>]#2/fn[execute]`) reads and records through `self.ctx` (`prepare_read`, `observe_edges_by`). It also runs the agent with `agent.run(request, self.ctx)`. So the agent's tools use the same `ValidationContext` as direct reads. `shared_context` is only cited, so it adds no further obligation here. The behavior after the call (recording fingerprints, starting each verification with an empty list) belongs to other declarations. No missing root or gap.\n\nbehavioral: Obligations in `requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.ValidationContext.ask`: (1) `ask::<R>()` starts an agent request whose submitted answer is decoded as `R`; (2) the request's graph tools share the dependency list used by direct reads. The `shared_context` requirement is cited, so I checked that it is applied here but did not reassess it.\n\nObligation 1 is covered by `crates/trust-but-verify/src/graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]`. It calls `ctx.ask::<Answer>()`, awaits the result, asserts `answer.n == 7`, and checks the request schema (`properties.n.type == integer`). `fn[later_lighter_agent_calls_preserve_the_contexts_existing_trace]` also decodes an `Answer` through an inferred `ask()`. `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/configured.rs#mod[tests]/fn[verify_returns_direct_and_tool_reads_in_one_trace]` decodes a `bool` from a submitted `{\"result\": true}`.\n\nObligation 2 is covered by `verify_returns_direct_and_tool_reads_in_one_trace`. The criterion reads node 42 directly, then calls `cx.ask::<bool>()`. The backend then serves a `read_node` tool call for node 7. The test asserts the returned dependencies are exactly [Node 42, Node 7], so tool reads and direct reads land in the same context. `later_lighter_agent_calls_preserve_the_contexts_existing_trace` adds that dependencies from direct reads and from agent selections (`contents_of_current_node`, `contents_of_successors`) accumulate in the same context's trace, in order. A later `ask` leaves that trace unchanged. `explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots` makes a similar check for the explicit insertions.\n\n`crates/trust-but-verify/tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` checks the public export inventory. It adds nothing needed for the behavioral obligations.\n\nThe tests assert the outcomes, and I found no unmarked relevant test and no uncovered obligation.",
